      "writtenOn": "2019-03-28T05:57:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "just realized that makes separation of data for certification analysis harder. Any \u0027application\u0027 like U2F that stores (k,v) pairs in flash will need to touch TPM objects when traversing the list, and vice versa. And we can\u0027t even say that operations triggered by U2F don\u0027t change TPM data objects 9and vice versa), since compacting nvram does move objects of all times, regardless of which application triggered it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "961d2908006ae1ddeb4728590806a583c8640a8c",
