      "message": "not sure if worth it, but: \nwe may decide to add/remove PCR digest algorithms in the future (e.g. drop all non-SHA256 since we don\u0027t use them). it probably makes sense to have .unique_index that identifies the digest in pcr_arrays[] and build reserved_index as NV_VIRTUAL_RESERVE_LAST + PCR_INDEX_START + pdsc-\u003eunique_index * NUM_STATIC_PCR + pcr_index; Then we can add/delete banks and add/ignore reserved pcr objects in nvram.\nsimilarly, we can reserve a whole block of object indices for PCRs (more than NUM_OF_PCRS) from PCR_INDEX_START to PCR_INDEX_END (\u003d_START + 144, for example, enough for 6 banks, still leaving 256-39-144 \u003e 70 indices for other reserved_data)",
